  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 26ffa32b781b3a465b82a930a597ac18, type: 3}
  m_Name: EnglishText
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DeepSeaDemo.DemoTextCatalog
  entries:
  - id: log01.title
    text: Routine Voyage Log
  - id: log01.body
    text: '12 June. The supply boat arrived half an hour early. Fresh vegetables
      at last. We checked the southern ladder and the winch; the sea was quieter
      than the training basin. Our new diver joked that this would be an easy posting.


      After
      lunch, the sonar operator found a repeating echo twenty-four metres below the
      platform. It sounded like someone tapping a steel pipe. Nothing was loose in
      the pump room. He marked it as a seabed reflection and promised another survey
      tomorrow. At dinner we called it our neighbour asking us to stop working.


      The
      echo returned after lights-out. There was no alarm. I wrote the time in the
      paper log because the terminal had already shut down: 23:17. Beyond the windows,
      the sea looked perfectly still.'
  - id: log02.title
    text: 'Night Shift: Equipment Faults'
  - id: log02.body
    text: '14 June. Array channel three failed at 23:17. The discharge pump tripped
      immediately afterwards. Both times are in the signed paper log. The exported
      alarm report says 00:03 the next morning: scheduled maintenance, no personnel
      risk. Nobody on this shift signed a maintenance order.


      The technician
      found dents pressed inward through the housing. Corrosion cannot explain them.
      When we shut the equipment down, the knocks stopped. When we tested the array,
      the echoes came closer. Nobody laughed this time.


      The supervisor says
      speculation is unprofessional. He wants the original records uploaded, and
      the paper copy corrected to match the system. I have kept this page unchanged.
      If these times are a clerical error, why does the report need to be replaced
      before anyone inspects the damage?'
  - id: log03.title
    text: Diver Observation
  - id: log03.body
    text: '16 June. Visibility near the outfall is collapsing. My flashlight showed
      a few metres of drifting particles and nothing beyond them. An empty beam does
      not mean empty water.


      My partner triggered active sonar. Something
      moved behind the pump frame. On the next pulse it was closer. We switched off
      the equipment and sheltered behind the rocks. It passed us and followed the
      pipe that was still vibrating. The metal groaned. For the first time, I could
      not tell myself it was just the current.


      We returned holding each other''s
      wrists. Do not scan continuously. Do not follow an echo into open water. A
      stone thrown against a distant metal frame drew its attention long enough for
      us to leave. Take cover first, make one decision, and then move. Sound travels
      much farther than our lights.'
  - id: log04.title
    text: The Unsent Report
  - id: log04.body
    text: '18 June. The company requested that we remove the contamination peak and
      submit last week''s water sample as this week''s result. I cannot sign that
      report.


      The submarine recorder still holds the original sensor timestamps.
      Discharge began before the alarm. The final images show the creatures striking
      the transmitting sonar array, then the discharge pump. They did not pursue
      the divers who had switched off their equipment and withdrawn. We described
      our fear as something evil in the ocean. We did not describe what we were pumping
      into its home.


      If you find this page, bring back the black box. Collect
      a fresh sample if it is safe. Compare the sensor log with the handwritten times.
      Do not rely on the company''s remote summary. Listen to the complete recording
      before deciding where the evidence should go.'
  - id: runtime.000
    text: Read the Routine Voyage Log in the safe room.
  - id: runtime.001
    text: Compare the alarm timestamps with the paper log.
  - id: runtime.002
    text: Pick up the flashlight from the equipment table.
  - id: runtime.003
    text: Confirm your diving suit at the equipment station.
  - id: runtime.004
    text: 'Enter the water. Right stick down: dive. Empty-hand Trigger: sonar.'
  - id: runtime.005
    text: Follow the pipes to the repair cage. Find the electronic lock tool. Outfall
      evidence is optional.
  - id: runtime.006
    text: Enter the flooded compartment. Read the last recording and retrieve the
      orange black box.
  - id: runtime.007
    text: 'Repair the submarine hatch: hold tool Trigger; judge the QTE with the
      other empty hand''s Grip.'
  - id: runtime.008
    text: Bring the black box back to the platform. Follow the blue return beacons.
  - id: runtime.009
    text: Insert the black box into the analysis socket. Review the evidence, then
      preserve or upload it.
  - id: runtime.010
    text: Investigation complete.
  - id: runtime.011
    text: Contaminated water. The flashlight reveals nearby surfaces. Sonar reveals
      outlines, but also reveals you.
  - id: runtime.012
    text: Checkpoint unavailable. Please start a new game.
  - id: runtime.013
    text: Equipment ready. Weather is deteriorating. Follow the yellow signs to the
      dive point.
  - id: runtime.014
    text: Hatch unlocked. The compartment is flooded. Watch your oxygen.
  - id: runtime.015
    text: Company Data Reception
  - id: runtime.016
    text: 'Uploading mission records...

      This is a fictional sequence. No real
      files are uploaded.'
  - id: runtime.017
    text: Automatic Cleanup Protocol
  - id: runtime.018
    text: 'Black-box copy: removed

      Local sensor index: removed

      Company
      conclusion: equipment failure. No abnormal discharge.'
  - id: runtime.019
    text: Last Recording
  - id: runtime.020
    text: 'Backup power restored. The recording shows the creature striking the active
      sonar array, then the discharge pump.

      It did not follow the divers who
      switched off their equipment and withdrew.


      The engine is making noise.
      Take the black box and leave.'
  - id: runtime.021
    text: Backup power is online. Take the black box and follow the return beacons.
  - id: runtime.022
    text: The checkpoint could not be written to disk. Retry is still available for
      this session.
  - id: runtime.023
    text: Destination obstructed. Movement cancelled.
  - id: runtime.024
    text: ' was moved to its recovery point.'
  - id: runtime.025
    text: DEEP SEA / THE UNSENT REPORT
  - id: runtime.026
    text: New Game
  - id: runtime.027
    text: Continue Checkpoint
  - id: runtime.028
    text: Settings
  - id: runtime.029
    text: Quit
  - id: runtime.030
    text: 'Quest 3 / Link or Air Link

      Grip: grab / Trigger: use or select'
  - id: runtime.031
    text: Investigation Paused
  - id: runtime.032
    text: Resume
  - id: runtime.033
    text: Return to Safe Position
  - id: runtime.034
    text: Retry Chapter Checkpoint
  - id: runtime.035
    text: Main Menu
  - id: runtime.036
    text: Comfort & Audio
  - id: runtime.037
    text: Volume -
  - id: runtime.038
    text: Volume +
  - id: runtime.039
    text: 'Turn: Snap / Smooth'
  - id: runtime.040
    text: 'Move Speed: Slow / Standard'
  - id: runtime.041
    text: 'Lightning: Standard / Gentle'
  - id: runtime.042
    text: 'Story Subtitles: '
  - id: runtime.043
    text: On
  - id: runtime.044
    text: Off
  - id: runtime.045
    text: ' (documents remain available)'
  - id: runtime.046
    text: Back
  - id: runtime.047
    text: FIELD ARCHIVE / READ AGAIN ANYTIME
  - id: runtime.048
    text: Close Record
  - id: runtime.049
    text: Black Box Decoded
  - id: runtime.050
    text: EVIDENCE CROSS-CHECK
  - id: runtime.051
    text: 'Black box: decoded

'
  - id: runtime.052
    text: 'Sensor: discharge preceded the alarm

'
  - id: runtime.053
    text: 'Sensor log: not recovered

'
  - id: runtime.054
    text: 'Water sample: abnormal contamination

'
  - id: runtime.055
    text: 'Water sample: not submitted

'
  - id: runtime.056
    text: 'Testimony: impacts stopped when sonar stopped

'
  - id: runtime.057
    text: 'Survivor testimony: not read

'
  - id: runtime.058
    text: '

      The creatures targeted sonar arrays and discharge pumps first.
      The company requests an immediate upload. Its protocol includes deleting the
      local copies.'
  - id: runtime.059
    text: Preserve Evidence / Refuse Upload
  - id: runtime.060
    text: Upload to Company...
  - id: runtime.061
    text: 'Ending: Case Closed'
  - id: runtime.062
    text: 'Ending: The Unsent Report'
  - id: runtime.063
    text: 'You followed the company''s instructions.

      The anomalies were classified
      as equipment failure.

      The platform resumed work. The echoes below did
      not stop.'
  - id: runtime.064
    text: 'You refused to upload.

      The evidence still connects the pollution
      to the attacks.

      The next person who enters these waters will not have
      to trust the altered report.'
  - id: runtime.065
    text: '


      Thank you for playing / Deep Sea Investigation'
  - id: runtime.066
    text: Start Again
  - id: runtime.067
    text: Return to Main Menu
  - id: runtime.068
    text: Confirm Upload?
  - id: runtime.069
    text: 'The company protocol will erase the fictional in-game records.

      This
      choice determines the ending.'
  - id: runtime.070
    text: Confirm Upload
  - id: runtime.071
    text: Back to Evidence
  - id: runtime.072
    text: 'Volume '
  - id: runtime.073
    text: Turning mode changed.
  - id: runtime.074
    text: Movement speed changed.
  - id: runtime.075
    text: Lightning setting changed.
  - id: runtime.076
    text: '

      Oxygen '
  - id: runtime.077
    text: '%    Acoustic Exposure '
  - id: runtime.078
    text: Pick up the flashlight from the equipment table first.
  - id: runtime.079
    text: Diving suit ready. Your oxygen gauge is on your glove.
  - id: runtime.080
    text: Place the matching item in the receiver.
  - id: runtime.081
    text: Release the black box into the socket. The evidence panel opens when playback
      finishes.
  - id: runtime.082
    text: 'Evidence registered: '
  - id: world.Alarm_Terminal.title
    text: Alarm Terminal
  - id: world.Alarm_Terminal.body
    text: 'Paper log: 23:17, sonar array lost and pump stopped. Digital export: 00:03,
      scheduled maintenance. Forty-six minutes are missing. No engineer signed the
      paper log. The discrepancy has been registered.'
  - id: world.Diving_Suit_Confirmation.title
    text: Diving Suit Confirmation
  - id: world.Diving_Suit_Confirmation.body
    text: Use an empty-hand Trigger to interact. Grip picks up physical objects.
  - id: world.Water_Sample_Receiver.title
    text: Water Sample Receiver
  - id: world.Water_Sample_Receiver.body
    text: Use an empty-hand Trigger to interact. Grip picks up physical objects.
  - id: world.Safe_Boarding.title
    text: Safe Boarding
  - id: world.Safe_Boarding.body
    text: Use an empty-hand Trigger to interact. Grip picks up physical objects.
  - id: world.Dive_Entry_Panel.title
    text: Dive Entry Panel
  - id: world.Dive_Entry_Panel.body
    text: Use an empty-hand Trigger to interact. Grip picks up physical objects.
  - id: world.Outfall_Sensor.title
    text: Outfall Sensor
  - id: world.Outfall_Sensor.body
    text: '23:11: discharge valve opened. 23:14: turbidity reached 8.7 times baseline.
      23:17: sonar array failed. The company export smooths this interval to normal
      values. Original sensor data registered. Return the nearby water sample for
      independent verification.'
  - id: world.Survivor_Transcript.title
    text: Survivor Transcript
  - id: world.Survivor_Transcript.body
    text: I could not see it. When the pump stopped, it stopped too. As we escaped,
      it turned toward the running array, not toward us. Do not erase the shutdown
      record. It explains why we survived.
  - id: world.Last_Submarine_Recording.title
    text: Last Submarine Recording
  - id: world.Last_Submarine_Recording.body
    text: 'FRAME 01: repeated sonar pulses. The creature turns toward the array.
      FRAME 02: the discharge pump ruptures. Divers escape while the animal circles
      the machinery. RECORDER: It follows the noise. This black box contains the
      original timestamps. Removing it will start emergency power. Follow the return
      beacons.'
